  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Due-date thresholds (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mDue soon and overdue. The clock moves, not the task. Needs a small scheduler plus a fired-set so alerts don't repeat.
[39m  [38;5;246mTells you something you didn't already know.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Activity log of your edits
  [38;5;246mA readable history of task changes. Nearly free once the append-only log exists, but it's a log view rather than a [39m
  [38;5;246mnotification — no real unread urgency.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] Status transitions you flag
  [38;5;246mNotify only on changes to specific fields you care about (e.g. a task moving to blocked). Meaningful even single-user
[39m  [38;5;246mif you script or bulk-edit tasks; adds a per-field interest rule.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Changes from other tabs/devices
  [38;5;246mRequires sync, which means the backend we just deferred. Would reverse the single-user decision — I'd hold this until
